    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0193" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg187"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.51/243: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tuck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-21T23:00:00-04:00">May 21, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>336. Your 727, May 18, 4 p.m., section 5,<anchor n="79" xml:id="d188-f1"/> per
                    first paragraph. In reply to a question at press conference today, the Secretary
                    of State answered: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“We have had up fully and freely the question of our deep concern for the
                            French people in their distress and in their conquered situation and our
                            great desire to see restoration of all of her popular institutions, all
                            of those rights and benefits and blessings that the great French
                            Republic once enjoyed.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d188-f1" n="79" xml:id="d188-f1-content">
                <p>Last two paragraphs of telegram.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
